{"pageProps":{"note":{"id":"e2hatetd17sm2887n0q8xtd","title":"2026-08-27","desc":"","updated":1787903283081,"created":1787839812834,"traitIds":["open-notebook-mvisani"],"custom":{},"fname":"open-notebook.2026.08.27","type":"note","vault":{"fsPath":".","selfContained":true,"name":"acol-dws"},"contentHash":"bc8077517eda103238a19e916869290a","links":[],"anchors":{"this-is-marcos-daily-open-notebook":{"type":"header","text":"This is Marco's daily open-notebook.","value":"this-is-marcos-daily-open-notebook","line":9,"column":0,"depth":1},"discussion-with-daniel":{"type":"header","text":"Discussion with Daniel","value":"discussion-with-daniel","line":11,"column":0,"depth":2}},"children":[],"parent":"tw9a0dj7e99t1uhlpv5zld3","data":{}},"body":"<h1 id=\"2026-08-27\">2026-08-27<a aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"anchor-heading icon-link\" href=\"#2026-08-27\"></a></h1>\n<h1 id=\"this-is-marcos-daily-open-notebook\">This is Marco's daily open-notebook.<a aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"anchor-heading icon-link\" href=\"#this-is-marcos-daily-open-notebook\"></a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"discussion-with-daniel\">Discussion with Daniel<a aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"anchor-heading icon-link\" href=\"#discussion-with-daniel\"></a></h2>\n<p>Big refactoring ahead.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>There should be a pure abstract class for both Y and Z such that we can use any implementation we want (I've already started on the Y one which is now stashed). </li>\n<li>Right now I should implement both a fully dense matrix for Y and Z. Y should contain a <code>std::vector&#x3C;uint16_t></code> in order to store the state and the counter. The Z matrices should contain a <code>std::vector&#x3C;uint8_t></code> in order to store the state only.</li>\n<li>We also want to change a bit the model. The Z matrices should also contain a state for the leaves. If I am not wrong then each tree's Z should be of size <code>n_nodes</code> times <code>n_leaves</code> of all other trees (to check) (or <code>n_leaves</code><span class=\"math math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>∗</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">*</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4653em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∗</span></span></span></span></span><code>n_nodes</code> depending on which tree it is). Previously it was <code>n_internal_nodes</code> times <code>n_leaves</code>.</li>\n<li>Then the Y state will be <code>n_leaves * n_leaves</code> and will be calculated as follows :\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P(Y_{ij}=1 | Z_s=1, Z_m=1) = (1-\\omega)^2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">P</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.22222em;\">Y</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.2222em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"siz